cff-version: 1.2.0
title: TissueTypist
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the associated preprint.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kanemaru
    given-names: Kazumasa
  - name: "Teichmann Laboratory"
abstract: >-
  TissueTypist classifies tissue niches in spatial transcriptomics data.
  It ships with a pre-trained cardiac classifier built on Visium SD
  (3-prime + FFPE) and Visium HD reference data, and adapts to other
  tissues via a single YAML hierarchy file.
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - tissue classification
  - single-cell
  - Visium
  - VisiumHD
  - Xenium
  - MERFISH
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Teichlab/TissueTypist"
acknowledgments: >-
  Documentation and code restructuring were assisted by Anthropic's Claude.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Developmental Dynamics of Human Cardiogenesis: A multi-omic reference and its disruption in Trisomy 21"
  authors:
    - family-names: Cranley
      given-names: James
    - family-names: Kanemaru
      given-names: Kazumasa
    - name: "et al."
  year: 2025
  journal: bioRxiv
  doi: 10.1101/2024.04.29.591736
  url: "https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2024.04.29.591736v3"
